            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-sanmiguel/recipes-sanmiguel/plat-svc/files/nic-snr-read",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd really like to avoid short-names like \"snr\" for \"sensor\"?  It's only a few more keystrokes and saves a lot of thinking on what \"snr\" means.  My first thought was \"signal-to-noise ratio\" which doesn't make much sense in context."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-sanmiguel/recipes-sanmiguel/plat-svc/files/nic-snr-read",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-sanmiguel/recipes-sanmiguel/plat-svc/files/nic-snr-read",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Why not just use pldmd for this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-sanmiguel/recipes-sanmiguel/plat-svc/files/nic-snr-read",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Potin Lai",
                        "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "potinlai"
                    },
                    "message": "Because the NIC PDR does not contain proper AUX naming information, the generated sensor names may not meet the naming rule requirements.\n\nWe are continuing to investigate using mctpreactor to configure the sensor names correctly. However, I noticed there are still several commits under review for adding `mctp-usb` support in mctpreactor. In addition, the NIC is a downstream device behind the SMA bridge, which makes the topology more complex and is not supported by the existing changes on Gerrit.\n\nConsidering the delivery timeline for enabling sensor readings for testing, I decided to use the `pldmtool` + `external sensor` approach as a temporary solution."
                }
            ],
